## Installation

Releases follow IGVF Catalog releases and are published to PyPI:

```sh
pip install {{{projectName}}}
```

Development builds track the catalog's `dev` branch and are installed from this repo's `dev` branch:

```sh
pip install "git+https://{{gitHost}}/{{{gitUserId}}}/{{{gitRepoId}}}.git@dev"
```

The default host is the API the package was generated against: releases use
`https://api.catalogkg.igvf.org/api` and dev builds use
`https://catalog-api-dev.demo.igvf.org/api`. Pass `Configuration(host=...)` to use another.

## Quick start

```python
{{^asyncio}}
import {{{packageName}}}

configuration = {{{packageName}}}.Configuration(host="https://api.catalogkg.igvf.org/api")

with {{{packageName}}}.ApiClient(configuration) as api_client:
    api = {{{packageName}}}.IgvfCatalogApi(api_client)
    genes = api.genes(name="ATF3")
    print(genes[0].to_dict())
{{/asyncio}}
{{#asyncio}}
import asyncio

import {{{packageName}}}

configuration = {{{packageName}}}.Configuration(host="https://api.catalogkg.igvf.org/api")


async def main():
    async with {{{packageName}}}.ApiClient(configuration) as api_client:
        api = {{{packageName}}}.AsyncIgvfCatalogApi(api_client)
        genes = await api.genes(name="ATF3")
        print(genes[0].to_dict())


asyncio.run(main())
{{/asyncio}}
```

Every endpoint is a method on `{{#asyncio}}Async{{/asyncio}}IgvfCatalogApi`, listed below. The interactive API documentation is at
[api.catalogkg.igvf.org](https://api.catalogkg.igvf.org/).

